From: mayi <3363523343@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(bf01): generate boot cache offsets and package images

[description ]:
- Generate BF01 timestamp slot offsets/sizes only for the dedicated
  SPI NAND labels and reject missing or mismatched companion slots.
- Copy and package both generated boot-cache images during BF01
  fastboot builds, preserving the existing yoc packaging flow.

[root   cause]:
- Persisting timestamp settings in Linux JSON does not make them
  available to RTOS before startup capture. FSBL needs fixed validated
  slot constants and factory images included in the normal build.

[JIRA      ID]:N/A (BF01 integration)
[chip project]:181x
[side effects]:
- Requires matching BF01 BSP partition/memory-map/RTOS/APP changes and
  FSBL preload support from 0046; generic layouts remain unchanged.
- SYSTEM shrinks by 512 KiB, while DATA keeps its physical offset/size
  but changes from mtd8 to mtd10. Regenerate boot and both rootfs slots;
  never truncate an existing SYSTEM UBI volume or reuse old mounts.
- The first upgraded capture needs a cache seed derived from the
  device's real saved JSON, or it will still use embedded defaults.
- No AI, capture, upload, live or A/B metadata policy changes.

[Affected *.ko/*.so/*.a] :cvipart.h, timestamp.bin, timestamp_bak.bin;
no .ko/.so/.a
[test]:
- BF01 fastboot and FIP builds packaged both cache images successfully.
- Isolated generator/CRC checks, existing offset/memory comparisons
  and generated DATA mount numbering passed; no board migration tested.

---

--- a/alios.mk
+++ b/alios.mk
@@ -34,6 +34,12 @@
 	${Q}cd ${ALIOS_PATH};echo "y" | yoc init;cd -
 	${Q}$(MAKE) -C ${ALIOS_SOLUTIONS_DIR} ALIOS_BOARD=""
 	${Q}cp ${ALIOS_SOLUTIONS_DIR}/yoc.bin ${OUTPUT_DIR}/rawimages/
+ifeq ($(call qstrip,${CONFIG_ALIOS_CUSTOMIZATION_PIPELINE}),cv1815ja_bf01_spinand)
+	${Q}cp ${ALIOS_SOLUTIONS_DIR}/out/timestamp.bin ${OUTPUT_DIR}/rawimages/
+	${Q}cp ${ALIOS_SOLUTIONS_DIR}/out/timestamp_bak.bin ${OUTPUT_DIR}/rawimages/
+	$(call raw2cimg,timestamp.bin)
+	$(call raw2cimg,timestamp_bak.bin)
+endif
 ifeq (${CONFIG_MIRROR_2ND_PACK_HEAD},y)
 	# prepend 128-byte "cimg" header (file_sz + chunk crc) so fsbl reads only the real image size
 	$(call raw2cimg_alios,yoc.bin)
--- a/tools/common/image_tool/mkcvipart.py
+++ b/tools/common/image_tool/mkcvipart.py
@@ -39,11 +39,22 @@
 def gen_cvipart_h(output, parser):
     logging.info("generating cvipart.h")
     parts = parser.parse()
+    timestamp_slots = [parser.parts.get(label) for label in ("BF01_TS0", "BF01_TS1")]
+    if any(timestamp_slots):
+        if not all(timestamp_slots) or parser.getStorage() != "spinand":
+            raise ValueError("BF01 timestamp cache requires two SPI NAND slots")
+        for slot, offset in zip(timestamp_slots, (0x08D80000, 0x08DC0000)):
+            if slot["offset"] != offset or slot["part_size"] != 0x40000:
+                raise ValueError("BF01 timestamp cache layout mismatch")
     with open(os.path.join(output, "cvipart.h"), "w") as of:
         of.write("/* this file should be generated by mkcvipart.py,")
         of.write("please do not modify this file manually*/\n\n")
         of.write("#ifndef CVIPART_H\n")
         of.write("#define CVIPART_H\n")
+        if all(timestamp_slots):
+            for index, slot in enumerate(timestamp_slots):
+                of.write("#define BF01_TS%d_OFFSET 0x%X\n" % (index, slot["offset"]))
+                of.write("#define BF01_TS%d_SIZE 0x%X\n" % (index, slot["part_size"]))
         env_exist = True
         env_bak = False
         param_exist = False
